From: Daeho Jeong <daehojeong@google.com>
Date: Fri Jun 6 11:49:04 2025 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM: f2fs: turn off one_time when forcibly set to foreground GC

one_time mode is only for background GC. So, we need to set it back to
false when foreground GC is enforced.

Fixes: 9748c2ddea4a ("f2fs: do FG_GC when GC boosting is required for zoned devices")
Signed-off-by: Daeho Jeong <daehojeong@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Chao Yu <chao@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Jaegeuk Kim <jaegeuk@kernel.org>

Bug: 325517257
(cherry picked from commit 8142daf8a53806689186ee255cc02f89af7f8890)
Change-Id: I24bae7bd907e0c2f2fba6fe880fa565e6354fd08
Signed-off-by: Daeho Jeong <daehojeong@google.com>

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common 71bd6942e33f9711a4cfc196a36102cbcef19ca8
Batch: B-1 (P4 stability & functional backports) - Class A, apply as-is; predicted ABI delta zero

---
diff --git a/fs/f2fs/gc.c b/fs/f2fs/gc.c
index eafb4ba335..b2cfc961ef 100644
--- a/fs/f2fs/gc.c
+++ b/fs/f2fs/gc.c
@@ -1910,6 +1910,7 @@ gc_more:
 	/* Let's run FG_GC, if we don't have enough space. */
 	if (has_not_enough_free_secs(sbi, 0, 0)) {
 		gc_type = FG_GC;
+		gc_control->one_time = false;
 
 		/*
 		 * For example, if there are many prefree_segments below given
